{"acceptance_length": 6.403846153846154, "acceptance_lengths": [8, 8, 8, 4, 6, 8, 8, 3, 3, 6, 8, 5, 8, 8, 2, 1, 8, 3, 2, 8, 4, 2, 8, 8, 1, 8, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 4, 8, 8, 4, 8, 8, 8, 7, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8], "accepted_draft_lengths": [7, 7, 7, 3, 5, 7, 7, 2, 2, 5, 7, 4, 7, 7, 1, 0, 7, 2, 1, 7, 3, 1, 7, 7, 0, 7, 1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 3, 7, 7, 3, 7, 7, 7, 6, 1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 19722425344, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 19722420224, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following relationships:\n\n1. **Samantha has 12 fewer paintings than Shelley.**\n2. **Shelley has 8 more paintings than Kim.**\n3. **Samantha has 27 paintings.**\n\nWe are asked to find **how many paintings Kim has**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Use the information about Samantha and Shelley\n\nWe are told:\n\n> Samantha has 12 fewer paintings than Shelley.\n\nLet\u2019s define:\n\n- $ S $ = number of paintings Samantha has\n- $ Sh $ = number of paintings Shelley has\n\nFrom the statement:\n\n$$\nS = Sh - 12\n$$\n\nWe are told that $ S = 27 $, so:\n\n$$\n27 = Sh - 12\n$$\n\nSolve for $ Sh $:\n\n$$\nSh = 27 + 12 = 39\n$$\n\nSo, **Shelley has 39 paintings**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the relationship between Shelley and Kim\n\nWe are told:\n\n> Shelley has 8 more paintings than Kim.\n\nLet\u2019s define:\n\n- $ K $ = number of paintings Kim has\n\nFrom the statement:\n\n$$\nSh = K + 8\n$$\n\nWe already found that $ Sh = 39 $, so:\n\n$$\n39 = K + 8\n$$\n\nSolve for $ K $:\n\n$$\nK = 39 - 8 = 31\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{31}\n$$\n\nKim has **31 paintings**.", "decode_seconds": 2.9164452622644603, "draft_calls": 52, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 64, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "4bca12596cde37b82da0567724939a4bcfb9a0c81eb0abfcbd264f6d37c89e34", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "cf8a7b5bae0f550c78d96fddf2b344e52624a5ca257e26c23ed9ee62435ed16a", "output_tokens": 334, "peak_allocated_memory_byte